# Validation meshes are regenerated by the matrix in a few minutes and are not
# worth 40MB of history. Only the exports a user actually prints are kept.
#
# Those kept ones go dirty after every matrix run, and it is not a real change:
# OpenSCAD's ASCII STL writer is not byte-stable across runs, so the same source
# re-exports the same part with the text formatted slightly differently. Checked
# on the 20T pulley -- 12712 faces, one body, volume identical to nine decimals,
# and the files still differ. Check the mesh before believing a diff here; the
# usual answer is `git checkout --` and move on.
projects/*/exports/*
!projects/*/exports/default_tile.stl
!projects/*/exports/fit_coupon.stl
!projects/*/exports/joining_keys.stl
!projects/*/exports/default.stl

*.stl.tmp
*.csg
*.deps
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/

# OpenSCAD editor/session cruft
*.scad.bak
.OpenSCAD/

# OS cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
